{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If it be found in your midst.</b> He used the expression 'in your midst' (בקרבך), and likewise at the end of the parashah: 'and you shall burn the evil from your midst' (ובערת הרע מקרבך), because the way of transgressors is to commit the transgression in secret. Therefore investigation is needed — one must search after transgressions committed in hiding and in places of concealment, and burn them out just as one burns out leaven from the holes and cracks of the house; and this is the sense of 'and you shall burn' (ובערת) and the expression 'from your midst' (מקרבך). And further it is possible to say that מקרבך may include מקרוביך — 'from your kin' — that is, 'and you shall burn the evil from your kin'; for if a person sees his kinsman committing a transgression, it is fitting for him to shame him by coming against him and that his hand should be first against him, and that he not spare his honor and not cover for him, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 15): ״וחרפה לא נשא על קרובו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:53.485871788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}